Autonomous Robot Using ROS2 Jazzy and Gazebo Harmonic

A complete implementation of an Autonomous Navigation Robot using ROS2 Jazzy, Gazebo Harmonic, SLAM Toolbox, and Nav2 Stack. This project demonstrates how a robot can create a map of its environment, localize itself, avoid obstacles, and autonomously navigate to a target location.

The project is divided into two major parts:

Obstacle Avoidance Robot → Robot detects and avoids obstacles automatically.
Autonomous Navigation Robot → Robot creates a map, understands the environment, and navigates autonomously to a goal location.
📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on building an intelligent robot capable of:

✅ Simulating robot movement in Gazebo
✅ Creating maps using SLAM
✅ Saving and loading maps
✅ Localizing itself in a known environment
✅ Planning paths autonomously
✅ Reaching destination points automatically

