⚙️ Installation
Step 1: Update System
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
Step 2: Install Required Packages

Install Navigation2:

sudo apt install ros-jazzy-navigation2 ros-jazzy-nav2-bringup

Install SLAM Toolbox:

sudo apt install ros-jazzy-slam-toolbox

Install TurtleBot3 packages:

sudo apt install ros-jazzy-turtlebot3*
Step 3: Source ROS2 Environment
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

(Optional: Add permanently)

echo "source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
Step 4: Verify Installation

Check Nav2 packages:

ros2 pkg list | grep nav2

Expected output:

nav2_amcl
nav2_bringup
nav2_controller
nav2_costmap_2d
...
🗺️ Phase 1: SLAM Mapping
Launch TurtleBot3 in Gazebo
Terminal 1
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger

ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py

Expected:

✅ Gazebo opens
✅ Robot appears

Start SLAM Mapping
Terminal 2
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger

ros2 launch slam_toolbox online_async_launch.py

Expected:

✅ SLAM starts

Open RViz
Terminal 3
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger

ros2 launch turtlebot3_navigation2 navigation2.launch.py use_sim_time:=True

Expected in RViz:

✅ Laser Scan
✅ Robot Model
✅ Map Generation

Move Robot to Build Map
Terminal 4
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger

ros2 run turtlebot3_teleop teleop_keyboard
Keyboard Controls
Key	Action
i	Move Forward
,	Move Backward
j	Turn Left
l	Turn Right
k	Stop
Goal
Move robot slowly
Cover the entire environment
Generate a complete map
💾 Phase 2: Save the Map
Terminal 5

Create maps folder:

mkdir -p ~/maps
cd ~/maps

Save map:

ros2 run nav2_map_server map_saver_cli -f ~/maps/my_map

Expected output:

Map saved successfully

Generated files:

my_map.pgm
my_map.yaml

Verify:

ls ~/maps
🧭 Phase 3: Autonomous Navigation
Stop Previous Processes

Press:

CTRL + C

Close all terminals.

Launch Gazebo Again
Terminal 1
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger

ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py

Expected:

✅ Gazebo opens
✅ Robot appears

Start Navigation with Saved Map
Terminal 2
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger

ros2 launch turtlebot3_navigation2 navigation2.launch.py \
map:=/home/kolhesatish-sde/maps/my_map.yaml \
use_sim_time:=True

Expected:

✅ Navigation Stack starts
✅ AMCL localization starts
✅ RViz opens automatically

Set Initial Pose in RViz
Click 2D Pose Estimate
Select robot position
Drag arrow in robot direction

This tells the robot:

“You are here.”

Send Navigation Goal
Click Nav2 Goal
Select destination
Drag arrow direction

Expected:

✅ Path planning starts
✅ Robot avoids obstacles
✅ Robot moves autonomously
✅ Goal reached successfully

📊 Expected Results
Robot successfully creates a map
Saved map loads properly
Localization works using AMCL
Robot plans shortest path
Autonomous navigation works
Robot reaches goal without collision
📚 Learning Outcomes

After completing this project, you will learn:

🔹 SLAM

Simultaneous Localization and Mapping for environment mapping.

🔹 Localization

Robot estimates its current position using sensor data.

🔹 Costmap

Robot identifies obstacles and free space.

🔹 Path Planning

Robot calculates the safest and shortest route.

🔹 Navigation2 (Nav2)

Complete ROS2 autonomous navigation stack.

🔹 Robot Simulation

Practical robot simulation using Gazebo Harmonic.

